;; Exact-once fire audit for the K==0 (VARIABLE-DISJOINT) self-join -- the
;; join_all_old / join_probe_old&lt;A,0&gt; cartesian path of the semi-naive fix
;; (docs/stats.md; docs/incremental.md §6/§8/§10).  stat_selfjoin covers the
;; K&gt;0 case (its two `path` clauses share `y`); this one covers the cartesian
;; case that shares NO variable, historically the shape most prone to
;; over-firing (see the earlier K==0 cartesian-join codegen bug).
;;
;; The recursive rule reads `r` in two body positions whose variable sets are
;; disjoint -- (r a b) and (r c d) -- so the join ordered after the delta driver
;; is a full cartesian (K==0) probed against R_old = FULL - delta.  Each
;; satisfying (r(a,b), r(c,d)) pair must fire EXACTLY once, not once per delta
;; variant it appears in.
;;
;;   r(a,d) :- r(a,b), r(c,d)   derives  FirstCols x SecondCols.
;;   Seeds r(1,2), r(3,4): FirstCols={1,3}, SecondCols={2,4}, so the closure is
;;   the 2x2 product {(1,2),(1,4),(3,2),(3,4)} (4 tuples) and stops growing.
;;
;; Hand verification:
;;   :25 facts rule            -> fires once.
;;   :26 self-join (K==0) rule -> once per (r(a,b), r(c,d)) pair = |r| * |r|
;;                                = 4 * 4 = 16 at the fixpoint.

table (r int int)

rule (r 1 2) (r 3 4)
rule (r a d) <-- (r a b) (r c d)
